body:
Thank you!

@jihyerish would you be interested in working on a pull request for the standard? (Otherwise I can work on this, but not until August or so.)

FYI @cdumez @gregwhitworth

It's not great to use "block" to refer to a viewport location and then use "start" and "end" to refer to the top / bottom of the viewport given "start" and "end" usually refers to an [inline direction](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes-3/#inline-base-direction).

It's not entirely clear what this means in a document in vertical writing mode, or more broadly any page that scrolls horizontally. In particular, it's possible for a document to have both horizontally and vertically scrollable. What does "start" of a viewport mean in such a page?

@smfr @grorg

@RByers 
In the past, while adding "center" to [ScrollLogicalPosition](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#enumdef-scrolllogicalposition) in CSSOM(see: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/81), there was a suggestion[1] to specify a boolean value which considers the situation whether or not the element is completely in the view like below:
```
partial interface Element {
      void scrollIntoView(ScrollPosition options);
    };

    dictionary ScrollPosition {
      float top = 0.5;
      float left = 0.0;
      boolean notIfViewed = true;
      long offsetX = 0;
      long offsetY = 0;
    };
```

The suggestion referred "[scrollIntoViewIfNeeded()](https://developer.mozilla.org/ko/docs/Web/API/Element/scrollIntoViewIfNeeded)" which is a non-standard feature. This API doesn't work if an element is already within the view. (As far as I know, it is still supported in Webkit.)
I'm not sure the boolean value, "notIfViewed" in this suggestion was reflected when updating [scrollIntoView()](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-element-scrollintoview) or [ScrollLogicalPosition](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#enumdef-scrolllogicalposition).
@zcorpan could you check out about this?

I think the use case that you mentioned above also could be supported by focus(), if scrollIntoView() can handle the condition when the element is already within the view, and [ScrollIntoViewOptions](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dictdef-scrollintoviewoptions) is added to focus() as a parameter.

[1] https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/www-style/2012May/0808.html, 
     https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/www-style/2012Jun/0455.html
